    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0629" n="619" xml:id="pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-13T11:00:00+07:00">November 13,
                            1945—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1969. Undated telegram from Stevens,<anchor n="19" xml:id="d466-f1"/> Peiping,
                    received today states that available local information indicates Communists have
                    intensified operations in Shansi and Suiyuan; Communists are converging from
                    several directions on Tatung, Kueisui is still under intensive infantry attacks;
                    Communist forces now encircling Kueisui comprising 36 regiments under Ho Lung
                    are reported to have stated recently that Communist forces will start large
                    scale civil war if Central Government refuses to accept proposed Communist
                    settlement of present crises.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d466-f1" n="19" xml:id="d466-f1-content">
                <p>Harry E. Stevens, Second Secretary of Embassy in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
